    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263">

                <pb facs="0754" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v11p1/pg705"/>

                <head>263. Telegram From the Commander of the Joint Task Force (Vaught) to the
                    Deputy Commander of the Joint Task Force at Masirah (Gast)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d263-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Wadi Kena</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1980-04-24T12:50:00+00:00">April 24, 1980, 1250Z</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Subject: Execute Order.</p>
                <p>Execute mission as briefed.</p>
                <p>We are ready and able. God speed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d263-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d263-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of Defense, Joint Chiefs of Staff Records, RG 218–07–0002,
                    Records of J–3 DDSO, Box 8, Iranian Hostage Crisis 1979–1984, I 380–458 Rice
                    Bowl JTF Message Traffic (22–25 Apr 80). Top Secret. Also sent to Beckwith, the
                    Deputy Commander of the Joint Task Force for Fixed Wing Air Operations at
                    Masirah, and the Deputy Commander for Helicopter Operations aboard the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nimitz</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
